# Chrome icon build (nightlife + traditional) — always

Reusable recipe for **FloqCAST**, **djBOT**, **VIP reserVIP**, and peers (ShoutOut). Local review assets under `images/chrome/` and `images/review/actual-icons/`. Not Search production until explicitly published.

## Canvas + ring

| Constant | Value |
|---|---|
| Canvas | `S = 1024`, center `(CX,CY) = (512,512)` |
| Ring radius | `R = 490`, stroke width ≈ 14 |
| Outside | `dist > 498…502` → pure black |
| Nightlife | Magenta→tiffany gradient ring (see `rebuild_ring()` pattern) |
| Traditional | Same interior/wordmark; **no** nightlife ring (or borderless square pack) |

Solid `#000` field inside the ring. **Ink-only wordmarks** — never an opaque plate/rect behind type.

## Type system (all chrome wordmarks)

| Piece | Spec |
|---|---|
| Font | `NotoSansDisplay-Bold.ttf` |
| Shear | `SHEAR = 0.286` (italic lean) |
| Stretch | After paint, height × **1.10**, then shear |
| White | `(255,255,255)` |
| Tiffany accent | `(0, 212, 254)` — final **T** (FloqCAST/djBOT/ShoutOut) or shared **V** (VIP) |

Protected brands stay as spelled: **ShoutOut**, **FloqCAST**, **djBOT**, **reserVIP** (mark reads `reser` + big `V` + `IP`).

## Ring intersection layers (critical)

When type kisses the ring:

```
layer 0  background  (black + interior graphic)
layer ½  under-ring fonts  (left tip / first letter(s) — ABOVE bg, BELOW ring)
layer 1  ring
layer 2  over-ring fonts   (right tip / accent T or IP — ABOVE ring)
```

Compose **only** as:

1. `base.alpha_composite(under, (left, top))`
2. `out = alpha_composite(out, ring)`
3. `out.alpha_composite(over, (left, top))`

**Never** flatten wordmark then draw ring on top of the whole string. **Never** leave old wordmark pixels in the base (they read as “stuck under the ring”). Hard-clear white/tiffany/green in the wordmark band + strip old ring before rebuild.

### Per-mark under / over split

| Mark | Under ring (left) | Over ring (right) | Accent |
|---|---|---|---|
| FloqCAST | **`F`** (full glyph, same-canvas shear mask) | `loqCAST` | Tiffany **T** |
| djBOT | **`d`** tip | `jBOT` | Tiffany **T** |
| VIP reserVIP | **`reser` + tiffany `V`** | **`IP`** | **V = 2 ×** reser/IP size |
| ShoutOut | left tip / `Shout` as needed | rest | Tiffany **T** on **OUT** |

Build under/over on a **shared upright canvas → one finish/shear**, then mask by letter (not a naive % width cut that clips a sheared **F**).

## Target sizes (current review chrome)

Baseline → apply user deltas with `round`; if ink width exceeds ring fit, **uniform-scale** the whole wordmark block to max width (keep proportions).

| Mark | Point / ink target | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| FloqCAST | body font ≈ **175–190**, ink h ≈ **200** (`FC_H≈200`) | Fit width ≤ **~720** if tips won’t kiss |
| djBOT | ink h ≈ **204** (= 170×1.20) | Set/robot up; wordmark under with gap, then kiss ring |
| VIP reser/IP | **X = 194** (= 162×1.20; 162 was 135×1.20) | **V = 2X = 388**; then fit width ≤ **~720** if needed |
| VIP furniture | Separate from type: scale lounge **×1.10**, nudge down; **do not** regenerate wordmark when only furniture moves |

## Placement (“kiss the ring”)

- Wordmark sits in the **lower** third; interior graphic in the **upper** ~60%.
- Nudge `top` so left/right ink tips reach ≈ **`R − 10` … `R − 2`** (into the stroke).
- Prefer a score minimize `|dL−(R−10)| + |dR−(R−10)|` with penalty if `d > R+4`.
- Max practical wordmark width ≈ **720–740** so both tips can sit on the lower arc without `dist > 502` clipping.
- Nightlife + traditional share the **same** wordmark pixels/placement; traditional omits the ring composite.

