## GIF (djBOT spin)

- Base still = new layout.
- Restamp **platter motion only** from a clean historical GIF (`eb8693d` nightlife spin).
- Map motion pixels onto the new turntable bbox; do **not** restamp the whole frame (avoids shearing the set / ghost **T**).
- After compose, wipe stray tiffany pixels **outside** the wordmark band (ghost **T** mid-icon).

## VIP furniture vs wordmark

- Furniture extract: red booth/chairs + table dark/highlights from lounge source; **do not** wipe chair legs (`y` wipe must stay below ~700 if source has legs).
- Furniture-only edits: extract/replace lounge; **copy existing wordmark ink layers unchanged**.
- Wordmark-only edits: hard-clear type+ring band with `keep_red=True`; rebuild type; keep furniture pixels.

## FIX PROMPT — rebuild nightlife + traditional chrome marks

Copy/paste when icons need a full rebuild:

```
Rebuild FloqCAST, djBOT, VIP reserVIP chrome (nightlife + traditional) per
.cursor/rules/icon-chrome-build.mdc:

1) Hard-clear old wordmark + old ring from base (keep interior graphic / VIP red).
2) Render type: NotoSansDisplay-Bold, shear 0.286, ×1.10 height, ink-only.
3) Accent: tiffany T (FloqCAST/djBOT) or V=2X (VIP). Sizes: FloqCAST h≈200,
   djBOT h≈204, VIP X=194 V=388; fit_width ≤720 if tips cannot kiss.
4) Split under/over letters (F|d|reser+V under; T|IP over). Compose:
   bg → under → ring → over. Traditional: same type, skip ring.
5) Place wordmarks to kiss ring (tips ≈ R-10). djBOT: restamp platter-only GIF;
   kill mid-icon stray T.
6) Write chrome + review actuals; bump icon-review-*.html ?v=; QA strip of all three.
```

Resume tokens: `@iconchrome$` / `$iconchrome@`.

## Do not

- Revert unfinished icon WIP to “ship furniture only” without re-queuing the open wordmark tasks
- Opaque plates / JPEG grey bands under type
- `jerseyCssBack`-style mistakes: photo/graphic must not be covered by a type matte
- Naive left-18%-width cuts that leave part of **F** over the ring
- Putting ring on after a flattened full wordmark (inverts F/T layering)
